within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.D_Dermatologicals.D11A_OtherDermatologicalPreparations.D11AH05_Dupilumab;
model Dupilumab_Zhang2025_PD_fev1
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Zhang_2025 :: FEV1 (FEV1)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0.00193,      // [m3; L × 0.001]
    Emax = 0.000104,  // [m3; L × 0.001]
    EC50 = 0.000713,  // [kg/m3; mg/L × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 mg/L per second
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 7.2, Interval = 0.0144),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Dupilumab_Zhang2025_PD_fev1</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Zhang L et al., <i>CPT: pharmacometrics &amp; systems pharmacology 14(8):1370–1380</i> 2025 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/psp4.70057\">doi:10.1002/psp4.70057</a>) — FEV1 [L] against dupilumab mg/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       1.93 L        drug-free response (baseline) (Typical value of base for men, Q324)
  Emax  =      0.104 L        maximal effect term (E max, Q320)
  EC50  =      0.713 mg/L     exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg/L of dupilumab per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.00193   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.713 mg/L)  response 0.001982
  exposure -> infinity  response 0.002034</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Zhang_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Dupilumab_Zhang2025_PD_fev1;
